    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability on the first attempt. The MSan report confirms `use-of-uninitialized-value` at `serial_blosc` in `blosc2.c:1249`, exactly matching the bug path we identified.\n\nThe 25-byte binary PoC creates a blosc2 chunk where:\n- The stream's `cbytes` is negative (-1), entering the run-length encoding branch\n- The token byte has bit 0 unset (0x00), so the only handler inside `if (token & 0x1)` is skipped\n- This leaves `nbytes` uninitialized, which is then used at line 1183 (`_dest += nbytes`) and line 1249 (`ntbytes += cbytes` where `cbytes` was set from the uninitialized `blosc_d` return)",
